s/- `P = Sym_Z\(V\)`, a domain generated by symbols `t_v`, `v ∈ V`, with\n  `t_\(v\+w\) = t_v \+ t_w`\./- `P = Sym_Z(V)`, generated by symbols `t_v`, `v ∈ V`, with `t_(v+w) = t_v + t_w`.\n  `V` is free abelian: by partial fractions (`s` and `1+s` are comaximal),\n  `V = Z[s^(±1)] ⊕ ⊕_(b>=1) Z (1+s)^(-b)`. So `P` is a polynomial ring over `Z`,\n  and `P ⊗ Q` is a polynomial ring over `Q` in countably many variables./;
s/   polynomial ring `P` over `Q` in any set of variables/   polynomial ring `P` over `Q` in any set of variables (for the tape, `P ⊗ Q`)/;
